    {
      "id": "claim_0df34b393fc24f87a830a0c9ee01c9d8",
      "statement": "An unparseable or unreadable settings file resolves to two empty paths rather than throwing, because the file is hand-editable and a typo in it should surface as a message about where Python is rather than as an exception out of an unrelated caller.",
